    "knowledge_point": "Finding the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Number With Positive Imaginary Part",
    "problem": "What is the complex conjugate of $z=3+5\\text{i}?$",
    "worked_solution": "To find the complex conjugate, we flip the sign of the imaginary part.\n\nIn the given number $z=3+5\\text{i},$ the imaginary part is $5\\text{i}.$ Flipping the sign, we get $-5\\text{i}.$\n\nTherefore, the complex conjugate is given by $\\overset{―}{z}=3-5\\text{i}.$",
